; The fork rule (issue 8): Weft_sim.run starts no OS domain and no OS
; thread, so the process can fork after a run. The test calls Unix.fork,
; so it is not in test/sim, where the test code must not call Unix. The
; guard makes sure that weft and weft.sim do not link the threads library.
; Windows has no fork.

(test
 (name sim_fork)
 (libraries weft weft.sim unix)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{os_type} Win32))
 (forbidden_libraries threads.posix))
